dts: rk3576-armsom-sige5: describe the secure world

Adds the two nodes Linux needs to talk to OP-TEE: the linaro,optee-tz
firmware node the tee driver binds to, and a reservation covering the
memory the secure world owns.

The address is 0x48400000. RKTRUST/RK3576TRUST.ini gives 0x08400000 for
[BL32_OPTION] ADDR, but that is an offset - Rockchip's fit_args.sh adds
CONFIG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE to any TEE address below the DRAM base, and RK3576's
base is 0x40000000.

The size is published nowhere, so it comes from OP-TEE itself, which prints
its layout as it starts:

  I/TC: OP-TEE version: 3.13.0-1034-g500b55c8a, fwver: v1.08
  I/TC: OP-TEE memory size: TEEOS 0x200000 TA 0xc00000 SHM 0x200000

0x200000 + 0xc00000 + 0x200000 = 0xe00000, 14 MB.

Both nodes are harmless in the default build, which ships no BL32: the SMC
goes unanswered so the driver does not register, and the reservation costs
14 MB of 8 GB. Without the reservation Linux is free to allocate over the
secure world - it happened to survive one boot here, which is luck rather
than a guarantee.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PBGQqVfXFDyZYA6aV3X3Qq

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-armsom-sige5.dts
@@ -1314,6 +1314,42 @@
 			#iommu-cells = <0>;
 			power-domains = <&power RK3576_PD_NPU0>,
 					<&power RK3576_PD_NPU1>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * Secure world. Only present when the bootloader carries BL32; a build
+ * without it leaves the SMC unanswered and the driver simply does not
+ * register, so the node is harmless either way.
+ *
+ * The region is Rockchip's rk3576_bl32 blob, loaded by SPL at
+ * 0x48400000 - the 0x8400000 from RKTRUST/RK3576TRUST.ini is an offset,
+ * and fit_args.sh adds CONFIG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE (0x40000000) to it. Its
+ * size is not published anywhere; OP-TEE reports its own layout at
+ * startup:
+ *
+ *   I/TC: OP-TEE memory size: TEEOS 0x200000 TA 0xc00000 SHM 0x200000
+ *
+ * which is 14 MB in total. Without this reservation Linux is free to
+ * allocate over it.
+ */
+&{/} {
+	firmware {
+		optee {
+			compatible = "linaro,optee-tz";
+			method = "smc";
 		};
 	};
+
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		optee@48400000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x48400000 0x0 0xe00000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
 };
